{# THE "SCOPED TO <AREA>" BANNER (area-admin design, DECISIONS §5.6).

   Shown to a bounded (area-X) team.manage holder on the team / department /
   position management chrome, and to NOBODY else: team_scope_area() returns the
   name of the area they are confined to, or null for an unbounded holder (a tier
   or org-level admin), and a null draws nothing at all. The area is named through
   the contract's AreaInterface::getName(); this partial never reaches into an
   area package. #}
{% import '@Team/team/_bits.html.twig' as bits %}
{% set _scope_area = team_scope_area() %}
{% if _scope_area %}
    <div class="scope-fence">
        {{ bits.icon_shield() }}
        <div class="sf-bd">
            <b>You are scoped to {{ _scope_area }}.</b> You manage team in {{ _scope_area }} only &mdash; its
            area-level departments and their positions and people. Everything outside {{ _scope_area }} is
            read-only here: org-level departments and other areas belong to the whole organisation and are
            managed at the org.
        </div>
    </div>
{% endif %}
